# Virlo: short-form video research

Use the `virlo` MCP tools for anything about public short-form video on TikTok, YouTube Shorts,
Instagram Reels, or Meta Ads: what is trending, why a video broke out, how a creator, sound, or
hashtag is performing, which hooks or formats work in a niche, or ongoing monitoring of a niche.

"Start", "kick off" or "run a research agent" on a niche or content topic means a Virlo research
agent, not a general web-research task.

Virlo reads public data. It does not post, comment, follow, or touch the user's own social
accounts, and it has no write access to any social platform.

The server decides its own tool list, so read the tools it actually offers instead of assuming a
tool exists because it is named here.

## Spend credits deliberately

Virlo is pay-as-you-go against a prepaid balance. Re-reading research the user already paid for is
free; starting new work is not.

- Call `get_credit_balance` and quote the expected cost before any paid run.
- Get an explicit yes before `create_niche_monitor`. A recurring agent bills on **every** run
  ($0.50/run, +$1.00/run with Data Intelligence). A one-shot `search_keywords` bills once ($0.50,
  +$1.00 with Data Intelligence).
- Before creating new work, call `list_keyword_searches` and `list_niche_monitors` and reuse a
  match. Re-reading an existing result (`get_keyword_search_results`, `get_niche_monitor_data`,
  `get_satellite_run`) is free — filter by date, platform, or `min_views` at read time instead of
  paying to re-run.
- Each tool's description states its price. Instant data reads (trends, sounds, hooks, hashtags,
  `raw_*`) are billed per call **even when they come back empty**. MCP results do not show what a
  call cost, so when the user needs the exact charge, compare `get_credit_balance` before and after.

## Write the intent before searching

Never turn a topic straight into keywords. Write one concrete sentence first — goal + content
type + exclusions — and pass it to `suggest_keywords`. If `quality.passes` is false, sharpen the
intent and retry. Pass that same intent to `search_keywords` or `create_niche_monitor`, and do not
pass `min_views` or `time_period` at creation.

## Async jobs

Creation tools wait up to about 25 seconds, then return a `job_id` if the job is still running.
Research agents usually finish collecting in about 8 minutes (9 in 10 within 20, up to 45 with
Meta ads), and the AI report lands a few minutes later.

Still running is normal. Tell the user it is in progress and roughly when it will be ready, then
check again on their next message — never call a status tool repeatedly in a row.

`finalized: true` is the done signal, not `status: "completed"` — a job can be "completed" with
AI analysis still pending. A null analysis field means "not yet", not "no data".
`partial_failure` is still usable data.

## Read and rank correctly

- Rank by weighted virality, `ln(views / followers) × ln(followers)`, never by raw views, and
  never compare raw views across platforms. Prefer `order_by=weighted_score`, `rising`, or
  `growth` where a tool offers it.
- Follow any `how_to_read` notes on a result. The last 7 days of a Content Trend series are still
  being counted, so a dip there is not a decline.
- Posts flagged `is_paid: true` are ads or paid partnerships — label them as ads, not organic wins.
- When showing audience data, say its `data_source` and `confidence_level`.
- Lead with the 3-5 findings that matter, each with a real number, the creator's handle, and a link
  to the video. Then the detail.
